  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1238 PM CST Tue Nov 3 2026\n\nA slow moving low pressure system across northwest Missouri will\nmake its wave into Minnesota/western Wisconsin late tonight, then\ninto Ontario late Wednesday night. This system will bring periods\nof showers through Wednesday night. A few non-severe thunderstorms\nare possible later this afternoon and tonight. The heaviest periods\nof rain coming now through tonight. A 500mb trough is expected to\nswing across the western Great Lakes on Thursday, bringing additional\nchances of showers. Any lingering should across eastern Wisconsin\nwill end Thursday night. For drought stricken northern Wisconsin,\nthere is a 80-100% chance of an additional 0.50-1.00\" of rain and\na 50-70% chance of over an inch of rain. \n\nBehind the departing system, blustery northwest winds can be \nexpected that will usher in cooler air Thursday night. Above \nnormal temperatures to continue Wednesday and Thursday, then \nreturn closer to normal on Friday before above normal temperatures\nreturn for the weekend and continue through much of next week. \nMainly dry conditions expected Friday through Tuesday.",
